{"name":"Death Guard","hex":"#9eb37b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"death","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The cessation of life and all associated processes; the end of an organism's existence as an entity independent from its environment and its return to an inert, non-living state.","Execution (in the judicial sense)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/death"},{"term":"guard","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who, or thing that, protects or watches over something.","A garda; a police officer."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To protect from danger; to secure against surprise, attack, or injury; to keep in safety; to defend.","To keep watch over, in order to prevent escape or restrain from acts of violence, or the like."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guard"}],"entries":[{"title":"Warhammer 40,000","blocks":[{"text":"Warhammer 40,000, is a British miniature wargame produced by Games Workshop. It is the most popular miniature wargame in the world, and is particularly popular in the United Kingdom. The first edition of the rulebook was published in September 1987, the eleventh and current edition was released in June 2026."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Keno_mini_wargame.jpg/330px-Keno_mini_wargame.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warhammer_40%2C000"},{"title":"Death","blocks":[{"text":"Death is the end of an organism's life. It is the irreversible cessation of biological functions that sustain a living organism. Entropy, nature's tendency toward disorder, can contribute to the breakdown of living systems over time. Upon death, organisms stop exhibiting behavior and generally begin to decompose through various physical and chemical processes. Death can occur at any stage of development, including in infancy. A person may experience clinical death that is reversible, resulting in some cases in a near-death experience. In humans, establishing death of the brain determines that an individual has irreversibly died."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Hendrick_Andriessen_-_Vanity_Piece_-_1914-DE_-_Museum_of_Fine_Arts_Ghent_%28MSK%29.jpg/330px-Hendrick_Andriessen_-_Vanity_Piece_-_1914-DE_-_Museum_of_Fine_Arts_Ghent_%28MSK%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Operation_Sci-Fi_Con_2015.jpg/500px-Operation_Sci-Fi_Con_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Operation_Sci-Fi_Con_2015.jpg/1280px-Operation_Sci-Fi_Con_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Operation_Sci-Fi_Con_2015.jpg/500px-Operation_Sci-Fi_Con_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOperation_Sci-Fi_Con_2015.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wh40k_painting_miniature.jpg/500px-Wh40k_painting_miniature.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wh40k_painting_miniature.jpg/1280px-Wh40k_painting_miniature.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wh40k_painting_miniature.jpg/500px-Wh40k_painting_miniature.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The assembly and painting of models is an aspect of the hobby as important as the game itself.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWh40k_painting_miniature.j